# Every text file is checked out with LF, on every platform. The catalog is built and
# published on Linux from LF files; a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true turns them
# into CRLF, and a local build then packages different bytes than the release build.
# Binary files are detected by git and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Stored with CRLF in the repository, and shipped that way by every release build: kept
# byte for byte, so declaring the rule above changes no published driver.
